1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:02,620
I'm Saming, Thear's old friend.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,410
You never told me about him.

3
00:00:04,430 --> 00:00:05,880
I'd completely forgotten he existed.

4
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:07,030
I only remembered when I saw him.

5
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:08,450
I'd love to take a trip
down memory lane.

6
00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:10,710
All talk, huh?

7
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:12,810
How about we settle this
with our fists, you bastard?

8
00:00:12,830 --> 00:00:14,080
You bet.

9
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:15,820
You always take
what belongs to someone else.

10
00:00:15,860 --> 00:00:17,420
Jeez, enough already!

11
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,760
You're both drunk.
Just go home already.

12
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:21,820
The Black Bull...

13
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:23,490
won't let themselves be caught easily.

14
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:24,940
The only way to catch them

15
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,120
is when they actually want to be caught.

16
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:29,820
I suspect that Saming is a mole
working for the Black Bull.

17
00:00:29,970 --> 00:00:30,870
(Provincial Police Training Center 5)

18
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,140
(5 years ago)

19
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:34,610
Endure! Don't waver!

20
00:00:34,630 --> 00:00:35,330
Louder!

21
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:37,930
Endure! Don't waver!

22
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:41,180
- All together now!
- Endure! Don't waver!

23
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:44,230
Endure! Don't waver!

24
00:00:44,410 --> 00:00:45,880
Squad, halt!

25
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:50,160
Everyone, right turn!

26
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:58,270
Wake up!

27
00:01:04,470 --> 00:01:05,490
Stand up straight.

28
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:07,060
Yes, sir.

29
00:01:17,990 --> 00:01:18,840
Hey, man.

30
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:20,050
Yeah, you.

31
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:21,930
I'm freaking sleepy.

32
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,360
I've never had to wake up
this early in my life.

33
00:01:26,550 --> 00:01:27,800
You just have to get used to it.

34
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:29,830
We'll be waking up early
like this for months.

35
00:01:32,830 --> 00:01:33,800
Who just yawned?

36
00:01:40,550 --> 00:01:41,680
Did you yawn?

37
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:44,560
Yes, sir.

38
00:01:45,270 --> 00:01:46,230
Are you sleepy?

39
00:01:47,390 --> 00:01:48,060
Yes, sir.

40
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:49,680
What were you doing last night?
Why didn't you sleep?

41
00:01:50,350 --> 00:01:51,430
I couldn't sleep, sir.

42
00:01:53,190 --> 00:01:55,010
Then I guess I have to wake you up.

43
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:02,530
Hey! Your friend is sleepy.

44
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,250
Get into push-up position!

45
00:02:09,050 --> 00:02:10,680
It's just a yawn.
What are we supposed to do?

46
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:13,420
Hey! Attention!

47
00:02:20,380 --> 00:02:21,240
What was that?

48
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,680
I'm asking you, what were you saying?

49
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:29,450
I was just saying that yawning
is hard to control.

50
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:32,300
We shouldn't be punished for it.

51
00:02:33,770 --> 00:02:36,210
It's your own body.
Why can't you control it?

52
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,830
Sleepiness, yawning, sneezing,
you should be able to control them all.

53
00:02:40,390 --> 00:02:42,060
If you can't even control your own body,

54
00:02:42,230 --> 00:02:43,600
then what the hell are you good for?

55
00:02:45,450 --> 00:02:46,470
As police officers,

56
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:48,930
are we forbidden from yawning
or feeling sleepy?

57
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Are you talking back to me?

58
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:54,070
Are you trying to be a smart-ass?

59
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:55,500
I'm not.

60
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:57,850
Just wanted to say how great you are.

61
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:00,010
You never yawn, never feel tired.

62
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,920
You're like a total superhuman.

63
00:03:02,850 --> 00:03:04,050
Permission to give you
a round of applause?

64
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:09,790
What's your name?

65
00:03:10,270 --> 00:03:11,180
It's Mungkorn, sir.

66
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:14,000
Mungkorn Phianwanich.

67
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:17,580
Mr. Mungkorn, are you sleepy right now?

68
00:03:17,630 --> 00:03:19,360
Yes, sir. But I can handle it.

69
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:21,870
I'm usually an early riser anyway.

70
00:03:21,970 --> 00:03:23,260
No, no, no.

71
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:25,210
Being an early riser doesn't matter.

72
00:03:26,110 --> 00:03:28,280
If you're sleepy, you get to sleep.

73
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:31,070
Coming to police training
is just like a vacation, right?

74
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:32,660
If you want to rest,
you should be allowed to rest.

75
00:03:33,710 --> 00:03:35,180
Of course, Mr. Mungkorn.

76
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:37,430
I'll make sure
you get all the rest you need.

77
00:03:47,050 --> 00:03:47,690
Run!

78
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:49,270
Run! Move it!

79
00:03:50,050 --> 00:03:52,800
Endure! Don't waver!

80
00:03:53,210 --> 00:03:55,980
Endure! Don't waver!

81
00:03:57,220 --> 00:03:58,760
Don't waver!

82
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:01,740
Endure! Don't waver!

83
00:04:01,870 --> 00:04:02,820
Mr. Mungkorn.

84
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:05,480
You can sleep in until noon.

85
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:06,820
Make yourself at home.

86
00:04:07,190 --> 00:04:09,100
I'll bring breakfast to your bedside.

87
00:04:13,930 --> 00:04:15,820
Damn, you're really picking on him now.

88
00:04:15,950 --> 00:04:17,020
It was just a yawn.

89
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:18,950
Did you have to make him lie
in the sun on the concrete?

90
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:21,190
The kid talked back,
for crying out loud.

91
00:04:21,550 --> 00:04:23,000
I just told them to do push-ups.

92
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:24,630
To wake them up.

93
00:04:27,610 --> 00:04:28,530
I like him.

94
00:04:29,090 --> 00:04:30,020
He's got guts.

95
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:33,260
The kid actually dared
to challenge your authority.

96
00:04:36,650 --> 00:04:37,960
You're into that?

97
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:44,060
Ugh, it's freezing out here.

98
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:46,150
Hey, it's cold.
I'm afraid you'll get sick.

99
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:47,110
Huddle up. Give each other a hug.

100
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:51,330
Hug him, too.

101
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,400
You love your friend, don't you?

102
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:04,440
Wow, you can actually sleep here?

103
00:05:20,790 --> 00:05:23,770
(Yin as Theartha)

104
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:31,430
(War as Mungkorn)

105
00:05:35,570 --> 00:05:37,920
(Shane as Phuwin)

106
00:05:38,350 --> 00:05:41,390
(Boss as Lukplub)

107
00:05:43,770 --> 00:05:45,500
(Kit as Kanin)

108
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:47,710
(Tang as Nadol)

109
00:05:51,190 --> 00:05:56,430
(Tae as Saming)

110
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:27,670
I looked up some info
on that rookie, Mungkorn.

111
00:06:28,430 --> 00:06:29,840
He's a kid from Phayao.

112
00:06:29,870 --> 00:06:31,060
His father was a veteran cop.

113
00:06:31,610 --> 00:06:33,240
So he wants to follow
in his dad's footsteps.

114
00:06:33,770 --> 00:06:34,540
Whoa.

115
00:06:35,550 --> 00:06:38,380
Do you like him so much that
you had to dig up his background?

116
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:40,960
Damn, we're instructors.
It's against the rules.

117
00:06:41,070 --> 00:06:44,100
Hold on, what do we call that again?

118
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:46,500
"An abuse of power"?

119
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:48,240
I know that.

120
00:06:48,670 --> 00:06:50,820
I'm just keeping an eye on him.
I haven't done anything yet.

121
00:06:51,490 --> 00:06:53,280
I'm impressed by the kid.

122
00:06:53,470 --> 00:06:54,790
I want to get to know him better.

123
00:06:54,890 --> 00:06:56,810
We'll see where it goes.

124
00:06:57,950 --> 00:06:59,050
Whatever floats your boat.

125
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,560
Not my type. Not at all.

126
00:07:01,910 --> 00:07:03,250
My type is over there.

127
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:05,450
Look at that tigress.

128
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:12,260
You really never stop
being a player, do you?

129
00:07:12,830 --> 00:07:14,030
I'm asking you seriously.

130
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:16,040
Is anyone ever going to
be able to stop you?

131
00:07:16,590 --> 00:07:17,650
No one, buddy.

132
00:07:17,810 --> 00:07:20,970
A guy like me was born to be a gift
to all the beautiful people.

133
00:07:22,710 --> 00:07:23,580
Good.

134
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:26,000
Then we won't have to compete.

135
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:31,580
So, anyway,

136
00:07:32,340 --> 00:07:35,020
is your dad going to
help you get promoted?

137
00:07:35,140 --> 00:07:37,860
You're lucky as hell.

138
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:39,410
Having a high-ranking father.

139
00:07:39,970 --> 00:07:40,990
Dammit.

140
00:07:41,370 --> 00:07:42,770
I don't take shortcuts.

141
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:44,610
I do everything by the book.

142
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:46,320
I don't use any special privileges.

143
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:52,260
Alright, get some sleep.

144
00:07:52,850 --> 00:07:54,530
We have training early tomorrow morning.

145
00:08:06,750 --> 00:08:08,580
What's wrong, Mungkorn? Can't sleep?

146
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,000
I'm just starving.

147
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:12,960
Man, same here.

148
00:08:13,390 --> 00:08:14,860
Dinner didn't fill me up at all.

149
00:08:15,590 --> 00:08:16,710
Who's talking?

150
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:18,560
I told you to sleep,
but you're still awake.

151
00:08:20,140 --> 00:08:21,350
You guys want to go for a run instead?

152
00:08:35,610 --> 00:08:36,400
Mungkorn.

153
00:08:36,940 --> 00:08:37,610
Mungkorn.

154
00:08:37,670 --> 00:08:38,300
Yeah?

155
00:08:38,940 --> 00:08:40,830
Let's head out.
Let's go find something to eat.

156
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:42,510
No way.

157
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:44,550
If we're caught sneaking out,

158
00:08:44,910 --> 00:08:46,280
we'll get punished again.

159
00:08:46,350 --> 00:08:48,480
We won't. I've done it before.

160
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:49,920
I know a shortcut.

161
00:08:50,270 --> 00:08:51,450
Please? Come on.

162
00:08:59,190 --> 00:09:00,220
Alright, fine. I'm in.

163
00:09:00,490 --> 00:09:01,190
Let's go.

164
00:09:02,130 --> 00:09:02,810
Let's move.

165
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,450
That's much better.

166
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:27,600
I really didn't get enough
to eat at dinner.

167
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:30,010
Totally. That lady's cooking was awful.

168
00:09:30,030 --> 00:09:31,260
Just imagine

169
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:34,860
if we had an egg and
some Vietnamese sausage...

170
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:38,050
Man, that would be a godsend.

171
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:39,710
Keep dreaming.

172
00:09:39,730 --> 00:09:41,040
Yeah, this will have to do for now.

173
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:44,340
But you know how it is, right?

174
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:46,910
Getting promoted in this
line of work is hard as hell.

175
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:51,270
If there's any shortcut,

176
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:52,500
I'll take it.

177
00:09:52,780 --> 00:09:53,800
Check this out.

178
00:09:54,270 --> 00:09:56,400
I went to see a shaman in Chiang Rai.

179
00:09:57,740 --> 00:09:58,540
Look.

180
00:10:00,450 --> 00:10:02,240
I got this sacred charm.

181
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:03,500
See?

182
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:05,870
No way, are you
really into that superstitious stuff?

183
00:10:06,110 --> 00:10:08,310
- Hey!
- I don't believe in that nonsense.

184
00:10:08,330 --> 00:10:10,050
I only believe in myself.

185
00:10:10,070 --> 00:10:12,950
I'm the one who controls my destiny.
It's my own rhythm.

186
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:14,940
Don't believe me? Watch.

187
00:10:15,410 --> 00:10:16,970
Check out my rhythm.

188
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,120
Really? Your rhythm.

189
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:23,770
Man, your rhythm is way off.

190
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:26,140
- I'm dancing for that tigress.
- You idiot.

191
00:10:34,490 --> 00:10:35,460
Hey, Saming.

192
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:36,140
Hmm?

193
00:10:36,390 --> 00:10:37,210
Sh*t.

194
00:10:37,830 --> 00:10:39,030
Isn't that the rookie
you got your eye on?

195
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:41,930
Is it?

196
00:10:43,550 --> 00:10:44,960
This is going to be fun.

197
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:47,500
Eating at this hour?

198
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:50,420
Hey, slow down.
Don't choke on your food.

199
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:51,670
Easy, guys.

200
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:55,380
You realize you're breaking the rules?

201
00:10:55,630 --> 00:10:57,630
Sneaking out of the dorm late
at night like this.

202
00:11:00,050 --> 00:11:01,320
We were hungry, sir.

203
00:11:02,010 --> 00:11:03,020
So we couldn't sleep.

204
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:04,690
I see.

205
00:11:05,070 --> 00:11:07,190
Couldn't control your own body, huh?

206
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:08,500
So you had to break the rules.

207
00:11:09,070 --> 00:11:09,820
So cool.

208
00:11:14,550 --> 00:11:16,820
How should I punish you guys?

209
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:20,070
Do you even have the right to?

210
00:11:20,550 --> 00:11:21,340
I sure do.

211
00:11:22,020 --> 00:11:23,380
I'm your instructor, after all.

212
00:11:24,070 --> 00:11:25,710
Aren't you guys off duty yet?

213
00:11:26,270 --> 00:11:27,900
And if you're still on the clock,

214
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:30,700
how can you justify drinking like this?

215
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:38,120
Well, we're off duty now.

216
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:39,600
Oh, if you're off duty,

217
00:11:41,550 --> 00:11:43,250
then what right do you have
to give us orders?

218
00:11:45,870 --> 00:11:48,890
Am I even supposed to follow them?

219
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:53,490
Watch that smart mouth of yours,
or you're going to regret it.

220
00:11:55,140 --> 00:11:56,990
You reek of booze.

221
00:11:58,390 --> 00:11:59,440
Regret what exactly?

222
00:11:59,890 --> 00:12:00,800
Go ahead and tell me.

223
00:12:02,820 --> 00:12:04,340
Thear, take it easy.

224
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:10,000
If the higher-ups hear about this,
we'll all be in deep trouble.

225
00:12:10,030 --> 00:12:11,660
That's a lot of empty bottles.

226
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:14,790
You've already had your dinner.

227
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:15,880
Aren't you full yet?

228
00:12:18,010 --> 00:12:19,910
I was the one who was still hungry, sir.

229
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:22,150
Mungkorn just came along
to keep me company.

230
00:12:22,630 --> 00:12:23,980
Please don't punish him.

231
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:26,660
Alright, it's fine.

232
00:12:27,730 --> 00:12:29,370
We'll let it slide this time,

233
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:32,080
but don't let it happen again. Alright?

234
00:12:32,910 --> 00:12:33,590
Yes, sir.

235
00:12:33,790 --> 00:12:34,780
Hey, Saming.

236
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,210
Aren't you being a bit too soft on them?

237
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,580
They're going to start getting cocky.

238
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:39,260
Man, just chill out.

239
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:40,720
The kids were just hungry.

240
00:12:40,750 --> 00:12:42,540
Don't go ruining
their futures over this.

241
00:12:44,950 --> 00:12:46,630
Alright, you two,
head back and get some sleep.

242
00:12:47,130 --> 00:12:49,410
Thank you so much
for understanding, sir.

243
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:51,010
We won't do it again, I promise.

244
00:12:51,050 --> 00:12:51,940
Thank you, sir.

245
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:54,210
Go on, move it.

246
00:12:55,930 --> 00:12:56,730
Hey.

247
00:13:01,650 --> 00:13:02,780
With an attitude like that,

248
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,730
you'd better watch out when
you run into the wrong person.

249
00:13:05,140 --> 00:13:07,040
Not everyone is going to be
as nice as we are.

250
00:13:08,850 --> 00:13:11,560
Thanks for the life lesson, sir.

251
00:13:12,930 --> 00:13:15,590
But when you get back,
make sure to drink plenty of water.

252
00:13:16,370 --> 00:13:18,030
It'll help with the hangover.

253
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:24,210
Let's get some sleep.

254
00:13:24,230 --> 00:13:25,690
- Come on.
- Let's go, man.

255
00:13:26,190 --> 00:13:27,040
Let's go.

256
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:28,450
Move it, buddy.

257
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:30,510
I think I'm going to have some
really good dreams tonight.

258
00:13:30,530 --> 00:13:31,910
Dreaming about who, exactly?

259
00:13:31,930 --> 00:13:33,090
You're in for it tomorrow.

260
00:13:33,110 --> 00:13:36,180
(Interrogation Station)

261
00:13:47,490 --> 00:13:48,370
Good Morning.

262
00:13:49,980 --> 00:13:52,670
You are the suspect,
Mr. Saming ChanJong, correct?

263
00:13:53,170 --> 00:13:53,990
That's right.

264
00:13:58,180 --> 00:14:01,930
You've been charged with theft.

265
00:14:02,030 --> 00:14:05,220
A report has been filed
stating that you stole a wallet.

266
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:08,030
Could you please explain
exactly what was taken?

267
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,740
No, I didn't steal anything.

268
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:12,830
How can you say that?

269
00:14:12,850 --> 00:14:15,980
The report clearly states that
you're the one who stole the wallet.

270
00:14:16,620 --> 00:14:18,390
And what evidence do you have?

271
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:20,810
I have plenty of money of my own.

272
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:22,560
I have no reason to steal at all.

273
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:25,820
Wait.

274
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:37,120
Don't give up yet.

275
00:14:37,150 --> 00:14:38,610
Keep pressing me. Hurry!

276
00:14:39,270 --> 00:14:41,020
Press how, exactly?

277
00:14:41,490 --> 00:14:43,030
You already said you didn't steal.

278
00:14:43,130 --> 00:14:44,610
And there isn't enough evidence.

279
00:14:45,070 --> 00:14:46,140
So that's the end of it.

280
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:49,570
Just try some small talk.

281
00:14:50,150 --> 00:14:53,630
I might relax
and slip up with some important info.

282
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:55,040
Okay?

283
00:14:55,090 --> 00:14:56,140
Alright.

284
00:15:06,450 --> 00:15:08,940
Did you know the victim before?

285
00:15:11,370 --> 00:15:12,800
Are you two dating?

286
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:13,740
No.

287
00:15:14,670 --> 00:15:15,900
I'm still single.

288
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:18,900
And do you live alone?

289
00:15:19,110 --> 00:15:19,950
Yes.

290
00:15:20,410 --> 00:15:21,900
I live alone.

291
00:15:22,330 --> 00:15:23,680
And I'm very lonely.

292
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:27,820
You must have plenty of money to spare

293
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:29,720
if you don't have to support anyone.

294
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:34,970
So, do you want me to look after you?

295
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,470
Are you a player?

296
00:15:36,490 --> 00:15:37,920
Oh, not at all.

297
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:40,200
I'm not like Thear.

298
00:15:42,050 --> 00:15:43,900
Hey, Instructor!

299
00:15:44,590 --> 00:15:45,500
What do I have to do with this?

300
00:15:50,570 --> 00:15:51,630
In that case,

301
00:15:52,610 --> 00:15:54,610
can you write something on my arm?

302
00:15:54,630 --> 00:15:55,930
Actually, never mind.

303
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:58,100
Write it on this paper for me instead.

304
00:15:58,810 --> 00:16:00,050
Write "Already taken."

305
00:16:03,730 --> 00:16:05,320
(Already taken.)

306
00:16:06,830 --> 00:16:07,650
Thank you.

307
00:16:16,910 --> 00:16:18,780
You're definitely the one who stole it.

308
00:16:18,950 --> 00:16:20,550
What? I don't understand.

309
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,890
Well, the owner of these bills

310
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:25,950
wrote "Already taken"
on every single one of them.

311
00:16:25,980 --> 00:16:27,150
On every single bill.

312
00:16:27,170 --> 00:16:28,980
And I checked the handwriting.

313
00:16:29,790 --> 00:16:31,090
It doesn't match at all.

314
00:16:31,710 --> 00:16:33,100
Wait, that’s not right.

315
00:16:33,220 --> 00:16:34,480
I've checked every single one.

316
00:16:34,510 --> 00:16:36,640
I didn't see that handwriting at all.

317
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:41,760
You just confessed that
you're the one who took it.

318
00:16:42,540 --> 00:16:43,890
So you checked every single one?

319
00:16:45,550 --> 00:16:46,350
Dammit.

320
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:49,120
I accidentally confessed after all.

321
00:16:50,510 --> 00:16:52,180
Catching me with my guard down?

322
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:55,620
Here.

323
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:57,300
A perfect ten.

324
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:01,630
Thank you, Saming.

325
00:17:02,770 --> 00:17:03,920
Everything you've taught me,

326
00:17:04,060 --> 00:17:05,950
I'll put it to the best use possible.

327
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:08,370
Did you just go easy on the kid?

328
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:10,540
Weren't you a bit too easy to trick,
Instructor Saming?

329
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:11,900
What do you mean?

330
00:17:12,020 --> 00:17:13,410
The kid is actually talented.

331
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:15,440
I just gave him a little nudge.

332
00:17:16,270 --> 00:17:17,660
You're that good, huh?

333
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:19,500
Care to teach me sometime?

334
00:17:19,950 --> 00:17:21,330
I'm the mean one.

335
00:17:21,830 --> 00:17:23,100
So no one really listens to me.

336
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:32,030
You did great.

337
00:17:32,060 --> 00:17:32,940
I almost failed.

338
00:17:34,030 --> 00:17:35,000
You're doing fine.

339
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:36,820
- Really?
- Yeah.

340
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,380
Mungkorn.

341
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:47,530
Actually, Instructor Thear isn't
such a bad trainer.

342
00:17:47,750 --> 00:17:50,230
But you're being
such a smart-ass to him.

343
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:54,440
But I think he's too full of himself.

344
00:17:54,570 --> 00:17:55,370
Hey.

345
00:17:55,890 --> 00:18:00,030
But I've heard rumors that
girls are all over him.

346
00:18:00,730 --> 00:18:03,720
I mean, just look at him.
He's got the looks and the money.

347
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:05,820
Man, even I'm getting flustered.

348
00:18:06,390 --> 00:18:08,400
He could have anyone he wanted.

349
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:12,330
No wonder he's so confident then.

350
00:18:13,970 --> 00:18:17,100
But he's really not my cup of tea.

351
00:18:18,690 --> 00:18:21,070
I prefer someone who's more humble.

352
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:40,140
Wait, Tri?

353
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:41,950
Where's my towel?

354
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:45,800
Hey, are you pulling a prank on me?

355
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:47,420
Hey, Tri!

356
00:18:48,590 --> 00:18:49,730
Is anyone there?

357
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:51,960
Hey, anybody! Is anyone there?

358
00:19:43,070 --> 00:19:44,340
What is up with you?

359
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:47,280
Are you some kind of creep?
Are you looking for an audience?

360
00:19:47,620 --> 00:19:49,020
I'm not trying to show off.

361
00:19:49,590 --> 00:19:50,630
My friends are messing with me.

362
00:19:51,510 --> 00:19:54,510
How is that tiny rag supposed
to cover you up?

363
00:19:54,530 --> 00:19:56,170
Here, take my towel.

364
00:19:57,220 --> 00:19:57,820
Go on.

365
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:02,460
If I let go,
I'll be butt naked for sure.

366
00:20:07,090 --> 00:20:08,630
Can you help me?

367
00:20:11,730 --> 00:20:13,120
Fine, have it your way.

368
00:20:32,970 --> 00:20:33,760
Thank you.

369
00:20:36,670 --> 00:20:38,410
I finally got a glimpse
of "Little Mungkorn."

370
00:20:38,430 --> 00:20:40,270
Hey, it's not "little," you know.

371
00:20:40,330 --> 00:20:41,700
I was just teasing.

372
00:20:49,260 --> 00:20:50,770
And why are you using this bathroom?

373
00:20:50,850 --> 00:20:52,180
There's an instructors' bathroom.

374
00:20:53,230 --> 00:20:55,030
The water in that one isn't running.

375
00:20:55,430 --> 00:20:57,490
So I came here to shower in peace.

376
00:20:58,890 --> 00:21:00,900
Funnily enough, I stumbled
upon a real treat.

377
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:08,530
If your friends prank you,
you should get back at them.

378
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,740
But then again, someone like you

379
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:14,500
doesn't seem like the type
to hold a grudge.

380
00:21:15,210 --> 00:21:18,150
From what I can tell, anyone who
gets close to you is bound to like you.

381
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:23,380
That's just how I am.

382
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:25,240
I like helping people,

383
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:27,990
even if it could get me into trouble.

384
00:21:29,640 --> 00:21:30,970
Just look at my friend.

385
00:21:31,380 --> 00:21:32,740
He betrayed me just like that.

386
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:38,710
I'll give the towel back right away.

387
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:42,140
Go ahead. I'll wait right here.

388
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:58,670
(Shooting Station)

389
00:22:22,050 --> 00:22:24,140
Hey, you've been aiming for ages.
Why haven't you fired?

390
00:22:26,340 --> 00:22:27,960
I was just adjusting my stance.

391
00:22:29,370 --> 00:22:30,450
Here, let me show you.

392
00:22:31,780 --> 00:22:32,520
Look.

393
00:22:33,210 --> 00:22:34,490
Step your left foot out a bit.

394
00:22:36,140 --> 00:22:37,490
Keep your shoulders relaxed.

395
00:22:41,410 --> 00:22:43,860
Why do you look even more tense now?

396
00:22:44,230 --> 00:22:45,430
I'm just not used to this, sir.

397
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:46,930
You're too close.

398
00:22:50,190 --> 00:22:51,550
When you're holding a gun,

399
00:22:52,230 --> 00:22:53,320
don't grip it with your whole hand.

400
00:22:53,760 --> 00:22:55,600
When pulling the trigger,
use only your finger.

401
00:22:57,260 --> 00:22:58,100
So the gun stays in place.

402
00:23:00,290 --> 00:23:01,040
Whoa!

403
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:04,270
Uh, Instructor Saming, sir.

404
00:23:04,980 --> 00:23:06,190
My gun is jammed.

405
00:23:06,220 --> 00:23:07,680
Could you please take a look?

406
00:23:07,710 --> 00:23:08,680
Yeah, I'm coming.

407
00:23:10,190 --> 00:23:11,540
Don't fire yet. Wait for me.

408
00:23:18,140 --> 00:23:19,600
Reload and keep firing.

409
00:23:25,700 --> 00:23:26,780
With a grip like that,

410
00:23:27,180 --> 00:23:28,740
you could shoot all day
and never hit anything.

411
00:23:32,150 --> 00:23:33,850
I'll just wait for
Instructor Saming to show me, then.

412
00:23:34,740 --> 00:23:35,940
It's not like I want to teach you,

413
00:23:36,400 --> 00:23:37,880
but watching you is just frustrating.

414
00:23:39,870 --> 00:23:41,370
Here, grip it tightly.

415
00:23:42,980 --> 00:23:43,870
Squeeze it.

416
00:23:44,580 --> 00:23:45,250
Okay.

417
00:23:47,120 --> 00:23:47,960
Aim carefully.

418
00:23:51,500 --> 00:23:53,050
Look at the target.
Why are you looking at me?

419
00:23:53,760 --> 00:23:54,830
Squeeze it tight like this.

420
00:23:55,120 --> 00:23:56,060
Relax here a bit.

421
00:23:56,080 --> 00:23:57,760
Okay, don't tense up your shoulders.

422
00:23:58,660 --> 00:23:59,440
Like this.

423
00:24:01,320 --> 00:24:02,920
In your stance,
put your left foot forward.

424
00:24:03,900 --> 00:24:04,730
Put your right foot back.

425
00:24:06,780 --> 00:24:08,040
There, squeeze it tight.

426
00:24:10,060 --> 00:24:11,580
Left side, lean forward.

427
00:24:12,300 --> 00:24:13,060
Yeah.

428
00:24:16,620 --> 00:24:17,350
Lean into it.

429
00:24:18,580 --> 00:24:20,040
The gun itself isn't dangerous.

430
00:24:20,220 --> 00:24:21,340
It doesn't just go off by itself.

431
00:24:22,020 --> 00:24:23,820
It's the person who lacks confidence
that's dangerous.

432
00:24:24,930 --> 00:24:27,970
Once the front and rear sights
are aligned, slowly pull.

433
00:24:28,890 --> 00:24:30,090
Slowly draw it back.

434
00:24:30,110 --> 00:24:31,490
Keep exhaling slowly.

435
00:24:35,150 --> 00:24:36,020
Slowly draw.

436
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:38,750
Easy.

437
00:24:39,970 --> 00:24:40,910
Exhale.

438
00:24:48,650 --> 00:24:49,330
Wow.

439
00:24:50,020 --> 00:24:51,240
Not a bullseye, but pretty close.

440
00:24:51,270 --> 00:24:52,440
You have a good instructor.

441
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,500
Oh? You can shoot now?

442
00:25:05,590 --> 00:25:07,420
Instructor Thear came over
to teach me, sir.

443
00:25:09,810 --> 00:25:10,810
It's not like I wanted to teach him.

444
00:25:10,830 --> 00:25:12,230
Watching him was
just getting on my nerves.

445
00:25:12,250 --> 00:25:13,430
His technique was a total disaster.

446
00:25:33,070 --> 00:25:34,540
Next time you need something,
let me know first.

447
00:25:35,610 --> 00:25:36,550
Thank you, sir.

448
00:25:40,160 --> 00:25:45,470
(3 months later)

449
00:25:45,490 --> 00:25:48,270
Hey, man, I got a really good amulet.

450
00:25:48,700 --> 00:25:50,620
Someone recommended it to me
from a temple in Chiang Mai.

451
00:25:50,930 --> 00:25:54,390
They say it protects you
and keeps all the bad luck away.

452
00:25:54,970 --> 00:25:57,120
And I even asked for a soulmate, too.

453
00:25:57,320 --> 00:26:00,460
I asked for someone with chubby cheeks
and a real cute face.

454
00:26:01,840 --> 00:26:03,240
I seriously can't believe it.

455
00:26:03,820 --> 00:26:05,510
I can't believe you've actually
become this superstitious.

456
00:26:05,880 --> 00:26:06,730
Count me out.

457
00:26:07,980 --> 00:26:10,140
My life isn't exactly unlucky.

458
00:26:10,240 --> 00:26:13,760
As for a soulmate,
I can find one myself.

459
00:26:13,890 --> 00:26:14,980
Just look at me.

460
00:26:15,760 --> 00:26:17,890
Hey, making merit
and praying once in a while

461
00:26:17,920 --> 00:26:19,530
isn't going to hurt anyone.

462
00:26:19,810 --> 00:26:21,710
Your birthday is coming up in two days.

463
00:26:21,850 --> 00:26:23,900
Want me to take you
to see a respected monk?

464
00:26:23,930 --> 00:26:26,090
Get a charm-enhancing ritual? You down?

465
00:26:26,250 --> 00:26:27,670
No way, man.

466
00:26:28,100 --> 00:26:30,550
My life is mine to determine.

467
00:26:30,570 --> 00:26:32,600
No being or god can decide my fate.

468
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:52,700
Hey, time to sleep.

469
00:26:53,120 --> 00:26:54,420
Hard training tomorrow.

470
00:27:36,660 --> 00:27:37,700
Where did your friend go?

471
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:40,530
I don't know, sir.

472
00:27:41,050 --> 00:27:41,910
Probably to the restroom.

473
00:27:42,280 --> 00:27:43,460
The restroom?

474
00:27:44,190 --> 00:27:45,840
Then why did he set up these
blankets to fake being in bed?

475
00:27:47,530 --> 00:27:48,900
He snuck out, didn't he?

476
00:28:43,190 --> 00:28:43,990
Where have you been?

477
00:28:45,440 --> 00:28:46,710
I went to the restroom, sir.

478
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:49,080
The restroom?

479
00:28:49,890 --> 00:28:53,180
I had no idea they started selling
snacks in the damn restroom stalls.

480
00:28:53,990 --> 00:28:55,060
Well, I...

481
00:28:55,090 --> 00:28:55,910
Well, what?

482
00:28:56,200 --> 00:28:58,660
I told you not to go outside, didn't I?

483
00:28:59,060 --> 00:29:00,310
Every place has rules.

484
00:29:00,520 --> 00:29:02,240
I'm responsible for your lives.

485
00:29:02,540 --> 00:29:03,600
If something happened to you,

486
00:29:03,620 --> 00:29:05,700
have you even thought about
what I'd have to do?

487
00:29:06,940 --> 00:29:08,250
Nothing's going to happen, sir.

488
00:29:08,830 --> 00:29:10,260
I can take care of myself.

489
00:29:10,280 --> 00:29:12,540
Brilliant. You think
you're just the smartest, don't you?

490
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:13,780
You've got a comeback for everything.

491
00:29:13,800 --> 00:29:15,180
But don't you dare
be a smart-ass with me.

492
00:29:15,490 --> 00:29:16,750
Rules are rules.

493
00:29:16,900 --> 00:29:19,410
If you don't want to follow them,
then don't bother being a cop.

494
00:29:19,440 --> 00:29:20,520
Just go home.

495
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:23,530
I was sent here to train you.

496
00:29:24,400 --> 00:29:25,850
If you refuse to follow orders,

497
00:29:26,030 --> 00:29:27,270
then I've failed in my duty.

498
00:29:27,850 --> 00:29:28,970
Don't blame yourself, sir.

499
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:30,500
It's my fault.

500
00:29:31,130 --> 00:29:32,560
You have no right to talk back to me.

501
00:29:33,310 --> 00:29:36,230
From now on, you will
follow my every command.

502
00:29:36,950 --> 00:29:39,470
Run fifty laps around the field! Now!

503
00:29:40,620 --> 00:29:41,420
Yes, sir!

504
00:29:42,620 --> 00:29:43,840
As for the rest of you,
go back to sleep.

505
00:29:52,590 --> 00:29:54,180
Act wisely!

506
00:29:54,650 --> 00:29:56,780
Always stay vigilant!

507
00:29:56,830 --> 00:29:57,840
Louder!

508
00:29:57,890 --> 00:29:59,320
I made a mistake, sir!

509
00:30:00,750 --> 00:30:02,230
I can't hear you! Louder!

510
00:30:03,690 --> 00:30:05,290
Act wisely!

511
00:30:06,110 --> 00:30:08,100
Always stay vigilant!

512
00:30:08,120 --> 00:30:10,710
- I can't hear you! Louder!
- I made a mistake, sir!

513
00:30:14,160 --> 00:30:15,730
- Speak up!
- Act wisely!

514
00:30:15,770 --> 00:30:16,710
What happened?

515
00:30:18,980 --> 00:30:21,150
The kid snuck out for food again.

516
00:30:21,170 --> 00:30:22,670
And what did he promise us both?

517
00:30:22,700 --> 00:30:24,100
That he wouldn't do it again.

518
00:30:24,750 --> 00:30:27,000
I lost my temper
and ordered fifty laps of running.

519
00:30:27,510 --> 00:30:29,080
Act wisely!

520
00:30:30,050 --> 00:30:32,160
Always stay vigilant!

521
00:30:32,560 --> 00:30:34,550
- Act wisely!
- Louder!

522
00:30:34,770 --> 00:30:36,890
Always stay vigilant!

523
00:30:37,060 --> 00:30:39,540
Maybe fifty push-ups
would've been enough.

524
00:30:40,650 --> 00:30:41,640
It wouldn't be.

525
00:30:41,750 --> 00:30:43,190
Do you really think
he'd learn his lesson?

526
00:30:43,410 --> 00:30:45,110
Act wisely!

527
00:30:46,640 --> 00:30:48,780
Always stay vigilant!

528
00:30:48,810 --> 00:30:50,000
I made a mistake, sir.

529
00:30:51,500 --> 00:30:52,680
Watch your volume!

530
00:30:52,890 --> 00:30:54,550
Act wisely!

531
00:30:55,380 --> 00:30:57,240
Always stay vigilant!

532
00:30:57,260 --> 00:30:57,900
Mungkorn!

533
00:30:58,160 --> 00:30:58,900
Hey.

534
00:31:00,670 --> 00:31:01,940
If you go in there to help him,

535
00:31:01,970 --> 00:31:03,110
what kind of authority will I have left?

536
00:31:03,480 --> 00:31:06,230
Do you want him to grow up to be a cop
who keeps making the same mistakes?

537
00:31:07,740 --> 00:31:08,950
I made a mistake, sir.

538
00:31:10,460 --> 00:31:12,050
Act wisely!

539
00:31:12,620 --> 00:31:14,790
Always stay vigilant!

540
00:31:15,670 --> 00:31:16,820
I think that's enough, man.

541
00:31:18,880 --> 00:31:20,640
It looks like
the kid can't take it anymore.

542
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:23,310
He's learned his lesson by now.

543
00:31:23,980 --> 00:31:25,790
If something happens to him,
it'll turn into a huge mess.

544
00:31:30,300 --> 00:31:31,730
Fine, it's up to you guys then.

545
00:31:32,430 --> 00:31:33,130
Hey!

546
00:31:37,560 --> 00:31:39,180
- Act wisely!
- That's enough.

547
00:31:39,420 --> 00:31:40,270
- Stop.
- Mungkorn.

548
00:31:40,560 --> 00:31:42,170
That's enough. You can stop now.

549
00:31:42,460 --> 00:31:43,580
Go on, go to sleep.

550
00:31:43,810 --> 00:31:46,410
No, sir. I have to finish them.

551
00:31:46,910 --> 00:31:49,680
Otherwise, people will think
I'm getting special treatment.

552
00:31:50,630 --> 00:31:52,170
It won't look good for all of you, sir.

553
00:31:52,740 --> 00:31:54,370
We know you've learned your lesson.

554
00:31:55,520 --> 00:31:56,320
No, sir.

555
00:31:57,060 --> 00:31:59,470
Since I've started,
I have to get through to the end.

556
00:32:01,790 --> 00:32:02,520
Mungkorn.

557
00:32:04,210 --> 00:32:05,790
Act wisely!

558
00:32:06,870 --> 00:32:09,470
Always stay vigilant!

559
00:32:10,800 --> 00:32:12,420
Act wisely!

560
00:32:13,340 --> 00:32:15,990
Always stay vigilant!

561
00:32:18,760 --> 00:32:20,260
Stand at ease!

562
00:32:21,640 --> 00:32:22,850
Don't look so lifeless.

563
00:32:22,870 --> 00:32:24,640
We have a lot more training to do.

564
00:32:25,510 --> 00:32:26,460
Stay sharp.

565
00:32:26,850 --> 00:32:27,790
Awake yet?

566
00:32:28,440 --> 00:32:29,680
- Yes, sir!
- We're awake, sir!

567
00:32:34,760 --> 00:32:36,010
And where is your friend?

568
00:32:36,260 --> 00:32:37,300
Why isn't he up for the morning run?

569
00:32:38,530 --> 00:32:40,770
Mungkorn is sick, sir.
He can't get out of bed.

570
00:32:45,430 --> 00:32:47,610
Hey, Saming, lead them for the run.

571
00:32:47,640 --> 00:32:48,800
I'll go check on him myself.

572
00:32:52,090 --> 00:32:53,050
Squad, attention!

573
00:32:53,870 --> 00:32:54,910
Right turn!

574
00:33:14,190 --> 00:33:15,080
Mr. Mungkorn.

575
00:33:24,270 --> 00:33:25,270
I'm sorry, sir.

576
00:33:25,750 --> 00:33:27,000
I overslept.

577
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:30,160
I'll go join the line right away, sir.

578
00:33:32,340 --> 00:33:33,290
Wait, hold on.

579
00:33:34,780 --> 00:33:35,790
Can you even handle it?

580
00:33:36,070 --> 00:33:37,710
Your friend said you were sick.

581
00:33:38,140 --> 00:33:38,920
I'm fine, sir.

582
00:33:39,300 --> 00:33:40,570
I'm feeling much better now.

583
00:33:42,320 --> 00:33:43,660
Don't talk back.

584
00:33:43,680 --> 00:33:46,410
I just touched you,
and I can tell you've got a fever.

585
00:33:46,720 --> 00:33:48,470
If I let you go run in the sun,

586
00:33:48,960 --> 00:33:50,240
you'll definitely pass out and die.

587
00:33:55,030 --> 00:33:56,110
Just stay in bed and rest.

588
00:33:56,860 --> 00:33:59,910
I'll go get some medicine
and a cloth to wipe you down.

589
00:34:00,400 --> 00:34:01,420
That's not necessary, sir.

590
00:34:02,700 --> 00:34:04,200
I'd rather go to the infirmary myself.

591
00:34:05,870 --> 00:34:07,390
You really are stubborn, aren't you?

592
00:34:08,160 --> 00:34:10,180
Just lie back and rest.
I'll take care of it.

593
00:34:38,620 --> 00:34:39,650
You really don't have to, sir.

594
00:34:40,240 --> 00:34:41,370
I'd rather do it myself.

595
00:34:42,790 --> 00:34:44,090
Just stay still, will you?

596
00:34:45,640 --> 00:34:47,050
I told you already

597
00:34:47,220 --> 00:34:49,120
that I'm responsible for your lives.

598
00:34:50,370 --> 00:34:51,840
It was my own fault, anyway.

599
00:34:53,480 --> 00:34:54,490
I'm sorry, sir.

600
00:34:59,600 --> 00:35:01,020
I hope you understand

601
00:35:01,040 --> 00:35:02,150
why I had to punish you.

602
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:06,730
I was sent here to train you all
to become police officers.

603
00:35:08,680 --> 00:35:10,740
So it's a huge responsibility for me

604
00:35:11,120 --> 00:35:13,030
to make your dreams come true.

605
00:35:15,030 --> 00:35:16,410
That's why I was so disappointed

606
00:35:16,810 --> 00:35:18,580
that I couldn't get you to listen to me.

607
00:35:19,690 --> 00:35:21,310
I understand everything now, sir.

608
00:35:22,980 --> 00:35:24,610
And I won't let it happen again.

609
00:35:26,650 --> 00:35:30,300
But at the very least,
I wish you'd be nice to me sometimes.

610
00:35:33,570 --> 00:35:37,220
Well, someone has to play
the tough and annoying part, right?

611
00:35:38,010 --> 00:35:41,210
Let Saming and Phuwin be the nice cops.

612
00:35:48,430 --> 00:35:50,440
Go ahead and eat that cake first.

613
00:35:50,820 --> 00:35:52,320
You need to have something
in your stomach before taking medicine.

614
00:35:54,460 --> 00:35:55,570
That's enough, sir.

615
00:35:57,820 --> 00:35:59,030
This cake?

616
00:36:01,370 --> 00:36:03,750
Actually, it's not for me.

617
00:36:05,500 --> 00:36:07,220
Yesterday was your birthday, right?

618
00:36:09,640 --> 00:36:11,420
And yet you still had
to come out and train us.

619
00:36:12,040 --> 00:36:15,090
I just wanted to do something small
to show my appreciation.

620
00:36:16,660 --> 00:36:18,420
That's why I snuck out
to buy this for you.

621
00:36:19,640 --> 00:36:22,680
But the shop only had banana cake

622
00:36:23,200 --> 00:36:24,740
and these prayer candles.

623
00:36:31,030 --> 00:36:32,150
Are you serious?

624
00:36:32,820 --> 00:36:34,350
Now, you're really
making me feel guilty,

625
00:36:34,370 --> 00:36:35,630
especially after I punished you.

626
00:36:37,740 --> 00:36:38,780
Not at all.

627
00:36:39,600 --> 00:36:41,590
You did everything right.

628
00:36:42,570 --> 00:36:43,630
By acting like that,

629
00:36:44,430 --> 00:36:46,020
I respect you even more now.

630
00:36:56,460 --> 00:36:57,130
Hey.

631
00:36:58,240 --> 00:37:00,430
Tri has been sneaking cigarettes.

632
00:37:01,140 --> 00:37:02,190
You should put him
through some extra drills.

633
00:37:03,540 --> 00:37:05,070
See? That’s more like it.

634
00:37:05,110 --> 00:37:06,330
He needs to get
a taste of his own medicine.

635
00:37:18,330 --> 00:37:20,040
Happy Birthday, Instructor Thear.

636
00:37:24,070 --> 00:37:25,470
Thank you, Mr. Mungkorn.

637
00:37:27,980 --> 00:37:28,950
Wait!

638
00:37:30,490 --> 00:37:32,060
Make a wish first.

639
00:37:33,370 --> 00:37:34,150
Oh, right.

640
00:37:34,680 --> 00:37:35,710
Alright, here goes.

641
00:37:36,340 --> 00:37:37,670
I’m not asking for much.

642
00:37:37,930 --> 00:37:41,100
I wish for a successful
career just like this.

643
00:37:41,560 --> 00:37:43,030
To find a great love.

644
00:37:43,270 --> 00:37:45,140
A cute, petite partner.

645
00:37:46,530 --> 00:37:47,580
And big boobs would be even better.

646
00:37:49,350 --> 00:37:51,050
Wow, you certainly have a clear type.

647
00:37:52,470 --> 00:37:54,560
Amen to that. May my wish come true.

648
00:37:55,650 --> 00:37:58,390
I think we should split it.

649
00:37:59,660 --> 00:38:01,700
No way. I bought it for you.
You should be the one to eat it.

650
00:38:01,730 --> 00:38:03,810
Come on, don't be stubborn.
Let's eat together.

651
00:38:05,510 --> 00:38:06,370
You have to take your medicine soon.

652
00:38:06,400 --> 00:38:08,380
So have some first,
so it doesn't upset your stomach.

653
00:38:11,980 --> 00:38:13,100
The rest is all yours.

654
00:38:13,860 --> 00:38:14,730
Thank you.

655
00:38:26,240 --> 00:38:27,930
I should've bought two.

656
00:38:31,030 --> 00:38:32,130
Oh, wait.

657
00:38:33,220 --> 00:38:35,320
I have one more thing for you.

658
00:38:36,010 --> 00:38:36,940
What is it now?

659
00:38:37,410 --> 00:38:38,150
Here.

660
00:38:40,850 --> 00:38:43,020
I was walking
through the market the other day.

661
00:38:44,840 --> 00:38:46,450
And I came across this coffee mug.

662
00:38:47,260 --> 00:38:50,380
It has the same pattern as yours,
just a different color.

663
00:38:50,410 --> 00:38:52,860
Here, you can alternate between them.

664
00:38:53,640 --> 00:38:54,550
Whoa.

665
00:38:56,810 --> 00:38:58,460
You really did all this for me?

666
00:38:59,240 --> 00:39:00,160
Thank you.

667
00:39:00,700 --> 00:39:01,820
Do you have a thing for me?

668
00:39:02,530 --> 00:39:03,970
Hey, I'm into people
with big boobies, you know.

669
00:39:06,140 --> 00:39:08,080
I don't. I just respect you.

670
00:39:08,910 --> 00:39:09,910
Why would I like you?

671
00:39:11,590 --> 00:39:12,460
Thank you.

672
00:39:45,920 --> 00:39:47,100
(Tower Jump Station)

673
00:40:04,740 --> 00:40:06,170
Do you remember what I taught you?

674
00:40:06,560 --> 00:40:07,710
I do, sir.

675
00:40:09,260 --> 00:40:10,340
Want a little nudge?

676
00:40:10,360 --> 00:40:11,410
No, sir.

677
00:40:14,020 --> 00:40:15,700
- Can Mungkorn go first?
- Hey!

678
00:40:17,650 --> 00:40:18,410
Off you go.

679
00:40:21,690 --> 00:40:25,270
Here comes Mighty Tri!

680
00:40:33,850 --> 00:40:35,160
You got this, Mungkorn.

681
00:40:35,700 --> 00:40:37,870
The harness is 100% safe,
so don't worry.

682
00:40:38,070 --> 00:40:38,690
Okay?

683
00:40:38,840 --> 00:40:39,960
I'll be right here watching you.

684
00:40:41,370 --> 00:40:44,040
If you're nervous,
just take deep breaths in and out.

685
00:40:44,300 --> 00:40:45,210
Keep your focus.

686
00:40:46,100 --> 00:40:46,940
Got it?

687
00:40:48,230 --> 00:40:50,330
My focus is out the window.

688
00:40:50,880 --> 00:40:53,080
Once you've jumped,
I'll take you out for a meal.

689
00:40:53,110 --> 00:40:56,310
Tell me whatever you want to eat,
and it's my treat. Okay?

690
00:40:56,580 --> 00:40:57,910
I don't want to eat anything.

691
00:40:58,380 --> 00:41:00,970
Right now, I'm so nervous I could puke.

692
00:41:03,110 --> 00:41:04,010
Want me to push you?

693
00:41:04,780 --> 00:41:05,900
No way.

694
00:41:06,260 --> 00:41:08,500
If you push me,
I'm going to drag you down with me.

695
00:41:10,530 --> 00:41:11,330
What's taking so long?

696
00:41:11,350 --> 00:41:12,580
(Is something wrong?)

697
00:41:14,540 --> 00:41:15,890
Yeah, just chill out.

698
00:41:15,920 --> 00:41:17,780
Let him get it together first.

699
00:41:19,030 --> 00:41:21,240
Ugh, if you're that scared,
just go home.

700
00:41:21,850 --> 00:41:23,030
(Go do something else.)

701
00:41:23,050 --> 00:41:24,700
(Why bother being a cop
if you're just going to get in the way?)

702
00:41:24,730 --> 00:41:25,860
You're wasting everyone else's time.

703
00:41:34,800 --> 00:41:36,310
Why do you have to yell at me?

704
00:41:36,340 --> 00:41:37,640
Can't you just speak to me nicely?

705
00:41:40,230 --> 00:41:41,630
I'm tired of coddling you.

706
00:41:41,820 --> 00:41:44,340
Why are you even here?
Doesn't look like you want to be a cop.

707
00:41:45,200 --> 00:41:46,290
I do want to be one.

708
00:41:47,600 --> 00:41:50,290
Then show me what you've got, loser.

709
00:41:57,140 --> 00:41:59,890
I, Mungkorn Phianwanich,

710
00:41:59,920 --> 00:42:00,920
am no loser.

711
00:42:32,220 --> 00:42:33,080
I did it.

712
00:42:33,890 --> 00:42:34,750
I did it.

713
00:42:36,060 --> 00:42:37,220
I did it, sir!

714
00:42:40,060 --> 00:42:41,650
I did it!

715
00:42:47,060 --> 00:42:49,360
Sorry, I got a bit carried away.

716
00:42:50,270 --> 00:42:52,060
I didn't think I could actually do it.

717
00:42:52,660 --> 00:42:53,590
It's alright.

718
00:42:54,130 --> 00:42:55,110
You did great.

719
00:43:32,170 --> 00:43:33,100
Excuse me.

720
00:43:33,120 --> 00:43:34,290
Mmm, you did well.

721
00:43:34,740 --> 00:43:36,180
- Thank you.
- Go take a break.

722
00:43:42,100 --> 00:43:44,320
Well, well, look at our star trainee.
What's up?

723
00:43:46,440 --> 00:43:49,260
Thank you for giving me
the courage to jump.

724
00:43:50,100 --> 00:43:52,050
I'm actually terrified of heights.

725
00:43:54,140 --> 00:43:55,410
I didn't really do anything.

726
00:43:55,700 --> 00:43:56,900
You jumped on your own.

727
00:43:57,790 --> 00:43:59,310
Well, you scolded me until I stepped up.

728
00:43:59,350 --> 00:44:00,490
That's why I dared to jump.

729
00:44:00,860 --> 00:44:01,980
I don't like being challenged.

730
00:44:02,650 --> 00:44:05,190
Yeah, I think we'll get along.

731
00:44:05,220 --> 00:44:07,280
Just like me.
I hate being challenged, too.

732
00:44:07,310 --> 00:44:09,340
If anyone challenges me, it's on.

733
00:44:12,220 --> 00:44:15,170
You really can't judge someone
based on a first impression.

734
00:44:16,080 --> 00:44:18,170
I seriously hated you at first.

735
00:44:18,690 --> 00:44:20,860
I thought you were such a poser.

736
00:44:23,840 --> 00:44:25,610
I'm still acting like one, though.

737
00:44:26,360 --> 00:44:27,300
So you like me now?

738
00:44:28,600 --> 00:44:29,830
I've started to figure you out.

739
00:44:30,690 --> 00:44:33,170
I can just let it go now.

740
00:44:34,650 --> 00:44:35,810
Are you insulting me?

741
00:44:38,650 --> 00:44:39,930
You don't have to like me,

742
00:44:40,520 --> 00:44:41,800
but just don't hate me.

743
00:44:59,620 --> 00:45:01,300
I'll go take a shower then.

744
00:45:03,240 --> 00:45:04,320
Go ahead. Get some rest.

745
00:45:07,160 --> 00:45:09,130
I told you I'd take care
of this one myself.

746
00:45:10,000 --> 00:45:11,520
So why the hell are you trying
to steal him from me?

747
00:45:13,060 --> 00:45:15,070
What are you talking about?
When did I ever try to steal him?

748
00:45:15,280 --> 00:45:16,410
It's pretty obvious

749
00:45:16,800 --> 00:45:18,290
that you're hitting on him.

750
00:45:18,310 --> 00:45:19,860
Even after I said I wanted him.

751
00:45:20,400 --> 00:45:21,950
Bullsh*t. That's not true at all.

752
00:45:21,970 --> 00:45:23,950
I'm just talking to him like
any other junior. It's nothing.

753
00:45:23,970 --> 00:45:25,250
Don't you dare lie to me.

754
00:45:25,880 --> 00:45:26,640
You

755
00:45:26,910 --> 00:45:28,650
have always loved taking
things that belong to me.

756
00:45:28,930 --> 00:45:29,940
You must be thinking that

757
00:45:30,240 --> 00:45:31,740
everything comes so easily to you.

758
00:45:32,150 --> 00:45:33,950
So you think you can just take
whatever you want from anyone.

759
00:45:34,520 --> 00:45:36,030
Both the job and the person I like.

760
00:45:36,370 --> 00:45:38,440
Damn, you've really lost it.
That's not it, man.

761
00:45:38,730 --> 00:45:40,070
I talk to all the juniors like this.

762
00:45:40,090 --> 00:45:41,230
I was just helping the kid out.

763
00:45:41,610 --> 00:45:43,110
I know your moves all too well.

764
00:45:43,360 --> 00:45:44,520
You'll be hitting on him in no time.

765
00:45:49,110 --> 00:45:51,160
I keep telling you,
I haven't done anything.

766
00:45:51,750 --> 00:45:53,490
But who knows what will
happen in the future?

767
00:45:53,530 --> 00:45:54,500
Take this, you bastard!

768
00:45:57,260 --> 00:45:58,080
You piece of sh*t!

769
00:46:00,460 --> 00:46:01,470
- What's going on?
- Mungkorn.

770
00:46:01,500 --> 00:46:02,750
You almost missed the main event.

771
00:46:02,780 --> 00:46:03,670
Look at that.

772
00:46:03,690 --> 00:46:05,130
The instructors are actually fighting.

773
00:46:08,830 --> 00:46:10,110
- You bastard!
- Enough, goddammit!

774
00:46:10,340 --> 00:46:11,790
Why the hell are you guys fighting?

775
00:46:12,060 --> 00:46:14,040
Have some shame.
You are instructors, for God's sake.

776
00:46:14,590 --> 00:46:15,430
Bastard.

777
00:46:15,720 --> 00:46:16,590
Let me tell you something.

778
00:46:16,620 --> 00:46:19,010
If you want something,
earn it yourself.

779
00:46:19,030 --> 00:46:20,220
Don't come asking me to back down.

780
00:46:20,250 --> 00:46:22,370
- You loser, you're so pathetic.
- Oh, listen to this prick talk.

781
00:46:22,390 --> 00:46:23,610
- Come on then!
- That's enough!

782
00:46:24,000 --> 00:46:25,400
Stop fighting already.

783
00:46:25,730 --> 00:46:26,890
You guys are friends, dammit.

784
00:46:26,910 --> 00:46:28,000
I'm not his friend.

785
00:46:28,910 --> 00:46:31,290
I'm not backing down to him ever again,
no matter what.

786
00:46:31,880 --> 00:46:33,580
You're just born lucky.

787
00:46:34,240 --> 00:46:37,290
And I'll do
whatever it takes to beat you.

788
00:46:38,260 --> 00:46:39,330
Just you wait and see.

789
00:46:45,070 --> 00:46:46,500
I bet they're fighting over someone.

790
00:46:47,040 --> 00:46:49,310
How hot must that person be
for them to be fighting like this?

791
00:46:49,710 --> 00:46:50,440
I have no idea.

792
00:46:50,460 --> 00:46:51,390
I'm really curious now.

793
00:46:54,280 --> 00:46:55,330
Who is it?

794
00:47:02,810 --> 00:47:06,380
(Graduation Day)

795
00:47:06,580 --> 00:47:08,720
I'm off. Good luck, Mungkorn!

796
00:47:09,120 --> 00:47:10,420
Okay, see you around!

797
00:47:23,540 --> 00:47:25,110
Heading home already?

798
00:47:26,530 --> 00:47:27,210
Yes, sir.

799
00:47:27,940 --> 00:47:30,030
I've been training for months.
I'm starting to get homesick.

800
00:47:30,560 --> 00:47:33,620
My mom's probably prepared
a huge feast for me by now.

801
00:47:34,680 --> 00:47:37,830
I hope you got something out
of training with me.

802
00:47:38,570 --> 00:47:39,690
I learned a lot, sir.

803
00:47:39,720 --> 00:47:41,870
See? I've picked up so
many combat skills.

804
00:47:44,340 --> 00:47:45,820
Take what’s good and put it to use.

805
00:47:45,850 --> 00:47:49,130
Leave the bad behind.

806
00:47:53,220 --> 00:47:54,860
I'll ask for your help sometime.

807
00:47:55,320 --> 00:47:57,020
Phuwin told me you're a quick learner.

808
00:47:59,230 --> 00:48:00,240
Of course, sir.

809
00:48:00,620 --> 00:48:02,450
You can call on me anytime.

810
00:48:06,540 --> 00:48:07,390
The thing is

811
00:48:09,190 --> 00:48:11,960
I saw you fight with Instructor Saming.

812
00:48:12,810 --> 00:48:14,500
They said it was over someone.

813
00:48:15,320 --> 00:48:16,280
Is that true?

814
00:48:19,320 --> 00:48:20,170
Fighting over someone?

815
00:48:20,760 --> 00:48:22,090
Nonsense. Fighting over who?

816
00:48:22,220 --> 00:48:24,610
We've never fought over anyone.

817
00:48:25,220 --> 00:48:28,100
Our types are completely different.

818
00:48:28,760 --> 00:48:30,490
It was just a stupid argument.

819
00:48:30,590 --> 00:48:32,820
Suddenly, it was like
he'd turned into a different person.

820
00:48:32,850 --> 00:48:33,880
Forget about it.

821
00:48:39,650 --> 00:48:41,800
Anyway, thank you so much.

822
00:48:42,970 --> 00:48:45,740
For making my dream
of becoming a police officer come true.

823
00:48:46,940 --> 00:48:48,740
I was just a small part of it.

824
00:48:49,150 --> 00:48:52,460
In the end,
it was you who made it happen.

825
00:48:54,080 --> 00:48:55,940
Oh, getting all humble all of a sudden?

826
00:48:56,180 --> 00:48:58,100
You weren't like this on the first day.

827
00:48:58,570 --> 00:49:00,300
Go on, show off a little.
Go ahead, brag all you want.

828
00:49:02,720 --> 00:49:05,480
People change, you know?

829
00:49:07,520 --> 00:49:10,030
I still have many sides
left for you to discover.

830
00:49:12,410 --> 00:49:14,840
♪When you smile♪

831
00:49:14,860 --> 00:49:17,270
♪And you look into my eyes♪

832
00:49:17,290 --> 00:49:21,600
♪It's too much for this heart
to keep inside♪

833
00:49:22,210 --> 00:49:24,610
♪Almost forgot how to breathe,♪

834
00:49:24,630 --> 00:49:27,090
♪How could you do this to me?♪

835
00:49:27,120 --> 00:49:29,840
♪Told you to stop,
but you wouldn't agree♪

836
00:49:29,870 --> 00:49:31,080
Well, I'm heading off then.

837
00:49:32,170 --> 00:49:33,140
Safe travels.

838
00:49:33,520 --> 00:49:35,140
I hope we meet again.

839
00:49:39,570 --> 00:49:44,450
♪That level of cuteness is
against the law♪

840
00:49:44,480 --> 00:49:49,090
♪I must be under your spell,
can I blame you at all?♪

841
00:49:49,380 --> 00:49:51,920
♪You're guilty of messing
with my heart,♪

842
00:49:51,940 --> 00:49:54,240
♪Stirring up my feelings
right from the start,♪

843
00:49:54,260 --> 00:49:57,180
♪The fine you'll pay
is your whole heart♪

844
00:49:57,610 --> 00:50:01,550
♪You take the blame,
I'll take the love part♪

845
00:50:03,760 --> 00:50:06,730
(Present day)

846
00:50:17,910 --> 00:50:18,810
Master.

847
00:50:19,800 --> 00:50:21,270
I want him to love me.

848
00:50:25,390 --> 00:50:27,080
You're too late.

849
00:50:28,700 --> 00:50:30,050
Because right now,

850
00:50:30,640 --> 00:50:33,120
his soul, his body,

851
00:50:34,090 --> 00:50:36,000
and his destiny

852
00:50:36,550 --> 00:50:39,810
are already bound to someone else.

853
00:50:40,500 --> 00:50:42,340
Then what should I do, Master?

854
00:50:43,940 --> 00:50:45,780
I don't want him to be with my enemy.

855
00:50:46,880 --> 00:50:48,480
Let me ask you one thing.

856
00:50:49,590 --> 00:50:50,990
Do you actually love him,

857
00:50:51,010 --> 00:50:54,480
or do you just want to win
against your rival?

858
00:50:55,380 --> 00:50:57,300
Both, Master.

859
00:50:58,380 --> 00:51:00,350
There might be a way.

860
00:51:04,210 --> 00:51:05,980
But are you willing to trade

861
00:51:06,010 --> 00:51:10,470
all the good luck
you'll ever have in your life

862
00:51:12,050 --> 00:51:13,430
for him?

863
00:51:19,180 --> 00:51:21,030
("An abuse of power"?)

864
00:51:21,050 --> 00:51:23,030
(I'm impressed by the kid.)

865
00:51:23,060 --> 00:51:24,460
(I want to get to know him better.)

866
00:51:24,480 --> 00:51:26,400
We'll see where it goes.

867
00:51:26,510 --> 00:51:27,610
Whatever floats your boat.

868
00:51:27,890 --> 00:51:28,970
Not my type.

869
00:51:30,470 --> 00:51:31,480
(You must be thinking that)

870
00:51:31,830 --> 00:51:33,320
(everything comes so easily to you.)

871
00:51:33,340 --> 00:51:35,180
(So you think you can just take
whatever you want from anyone.)

872
00:51:35,690 --> 00:51:37,250
(Both the job and the person I like.)

873
00:51:37,270 --> 00:51:38,580
Stop fighting, dammit.

874
00:51:38,980 --> 00:51:40,150
You guys are friends.

875
00:51:40,180 --> 00:51:41,260
I'm not his friend.

876
00:51:41,730 --> 00:51:43,430
You're just born lucky.

877
00:51:44,120 --> 00:51:47,120
And I'll do
whatever it takes to beat you.

878
00:51:48,350 --> 00:51:49,400
Are you okay?

879
00:51:50,070 --> 00:51:51,180
You could stay at my place.

880
00:51:51,210 --> 00:51:52,750
No, thanks. I don't want to impose.

881
00:51:52,770 --> 00:51:54,420
You're not imposing. Let's go.

882
00:51:54,920 --> 00:51:55,930
Let go of him.

883
00:51:56,240 --> 00:51:57,370
Leave him to me.

884
00:51:57,390 --> 00:51:58,700
What right do you have
to tell him what to do?

885
00:51:59,000 --> 00:52:00,350
It's after work hours.

886
00:52:00,380 --> 00:52:02,100
Are you his boss or his husband?

887
00:52:04,010 --> 00:52:04,970
Come with me.

888
00:52:05,000 --> 00:52:06,440
Jeez, enough already!

889
00:52:06,460 --> 00:52:07,540
I'll leave on my own.

890
00:52:34,110 --> 00:52:36,390
What did he do
to make you change your mind suddenly?

891
00:52:36,420 --> 00:52:37,460
But it's like...

892
00:52:37,490 --> 00:52:39,350
He's under some kind of spell, right?

893
00:52:40,180 --> 00:52:43,170
The dark magic will consume Mungkorn,

894
00:52:43,190 --> 00:52:44,930
and he'll forget who you are.

895
00:52:44,950 --> 00:52:46,720
You f*cking played dirty.

896
00:52:46,750 --> 00:52:47,680
Stay away from Saming!

897
00:52:47,700 --> 00:52:49,110
If Saming gets to sleep
with Mungkorn tonight,

898
00:52:49,130 --> 00:52:50,320
I don't think
things will end well for Mungkorn.

899
00:52:50,340 --> 00:52:52,740
I'll try to make him remember
one more time.

900
00:52:55,320 --> 00:52:58,630
♪Let's stop wasting any more time,♪

901
00:52:59,020 --> 00:53:02,050
♪Avoiding it won't make things right♪

902
00:53:02,260 --> 00:53:04,150
♪Just end this, alright?♪

903
00:53:04,180 --> 00:53:07,160
♪Say I'm no longer the one in sight♪

904
00:53:07,190 --> 00:53:09,920
♪And that I've lost this fight♪

905
00:53:10,210 --> 00:53:14,070
♪Just say it,
what are you waiting for?♪

906
00:53:14,100 --> 00:53:18,280
♪Tell me it's over,
and I'll walk out the door♪

907
00:53:20,810 --> 00:53:25,310
♪Don't keep me guessing anymore♪

908
00:53:25,340 --> 00:53:28,380
♪Say it and let me go♪

909
00:53:28,410 --> 00:53:32,260
♪Tell me all I need to know♪

910
00:53:34,400 --> 00:53:38,720
♪Don't keep me hanging anymore♪
